{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flowercomputers/bogkit/pulls/8","id":4134271815,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTVpH8872a_tH","html_url":"https://github.com/flowercomputers/bogkit/pull/8","diff_url":"https://github.com/flowercomputers/bogkit/pull/8.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/flowercomputers/bogkit/pull/8.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flowercomputers/bogkit/issues/8","number":8,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add Untitled Mobile FPS hackathon submission","user":{"login":"rcrdlbl","id":40729534,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzI5NTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40729534?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcrdlbl","html_url":"https://github.com/rcrdlbl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcrdlbl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcrdlbl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcrdlbl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcrdlbl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcrdlbl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcrdlbl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcrdlbl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcrdlbl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcrdlbl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Hackathon submission\n\nfork this repo, build your project (ideally via `./scripts/new-project.sh [project-name]`), then open a pr against upstream to acknowledge your entry.\n\n### category\n\npick **one**:\n\n- [ ] agent support\n- [ ] performance\n- [x] novel interface / gaming\n\n### team\n\n- **project name:** Untitled Mobile FPS\n- **team / author name(s):** rcrdlbl\n- **contact (optional):** @rcrdlbl\n\n### what you built\n\nAn iOS 17+ rear-camera multiplayer finger-gun FPS. Apple Vision recognizes the pose, calibrated aim, and thumb-down trigger; the game adds appearance enrollment, live person segmentation, UWB proximity, social/match flows, and a server-authoritative three-hit loop.\n\nThe Rust backend uses Fold materializations for accounts, social state, matches, events, history, and idempotency; ESE plus Fold BM25 for outfit text; and ANNy-backed HNSW indices for semantic descriptions, non-face whole-body embeddings, and nearby presence.\n\n### how to run\n\n```bash\n# from repo root\ncargo run -p untitled-mobile-fps\n```\n\nThe service listens on `0.0.0.0:3000` by default. Optional configuration: `FPS_PORT`, `FPS_DATA_DIR`, `FPS_SERVER_NAME`, `FPS_ENVIRONMENT`, and `FPS_MINIMUM_CLIENT_VERSION`.\n\nFor the mobile client, run `pod install` from `examples/untitled-mobile-fps`, open `UntitledMobileFPS.xcworkspace`, and deploy the `UntitledMobileFPS` scheme to an iPhone running iOS 17 or later. Use the Mac's LAN URL as a custom server on a physical phone.\n\n### demo / notes\n\n- Redacted live server inspector: <http://127.0.0.1:3000/inspector>\n- Standalone project history and detailed documentation: <https://github.com/rcrdlbl/untitled-mobile-fps>\n- The deterministic `fps-bot` binary supports a complete one-person match demo; see `examples/untitled-mobile-fps/docs/PHASE_2_TESTING.md`.\n- The portable Swift suite passes 111 tests. Camera, UWB, and gesture ergonomics require physical iPhone verification.\n\n### checklist\n\n- [x] i forked bog-kit and built my project in this fork\n- [x] my project is runnable from this pr (crate name and run command above)\n- [x] i selected exactly one category\n- [x] this pr is my official hackathon submission acknowledgment\n","created_at":"2026-07-25T23:10:55Z","updated_at":"2026-08-16T13:52:24Z","closed_at":"2026-08-16T13:52:24Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"fa98049ba6484501be7f8e9f4d982255d634691d","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flowercomputers/bogkit/pulls